  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/onsir/Trigonella_foenum_graecum_BelowLD50Dose">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="N1a39cf693cd54aec94dd2499dc11e6da"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/onsir/BelowReportedLD50"/>
    <rdfs:comment>Dose window for Trigonella foenum-graecum, bounded by the statistics its source reports.</rdfs:comment>
    <dct:source>Patel et al. 2017, J. AgriSearch 4(4):237-241, doi:10.21921/jas.v4i04.10200</dct:source>
    <onsir:boundQualifier>The source states that the LD50 is close to 350 Gy, its highest dose, at which 64 % of seeds germinated and 56 % of seedlings survived, against 96 % and 90 % in the control. 350 Gy is encoded as a lower bound on the LD50, so only the window below it is defined.</onsir:boundQualifier>
    <skos:scopeNote>The source irradiated doses from 150 to 350 Gy; where the window extends past them, the position is arithmetic only.</skos:scopeNote>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Trigonella foenum-graecum below LD50 dose</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/onsir/BelowReportedFavourableBand">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:definition>A DoseAssessment whose dose is below the lower end of the favourable band reported for its taxon.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/onsir/DoseAssessment"/>
    <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/onsir/AtOrAboveReportedLD50"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">below reported favourable band</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.org/dc/terms/title">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/onsir/Vigna_unguiculata_AtOrAboveLD50Dose">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="N442aeb831948480aaef37a9d91f16434"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/onsir/AtOrAboveReportedLD50"/>
    <rdfs:comment>Dose window for Vigna unguiculata, bounded by the statistics its source reports.</rdfs:comment>
    <dct:source>Gnankambary et al. 2019, Int. J. Genet. Mol. Biol. 11(2):29-33, doi:10.5897/IJGMB2019.0174</dct:source>
    <onsir:boundQualifier>Median of three genotype survival LD50s (129.8, 132.0, 150.2 Gy), each from a straight line fitted to survival at 50 % flowering relative to the control; observed survival at 150 Gy, the lowest dose tested, was 56 to 71 % and at 250 Gy zero, so the observations place two of the LD50s between 150 and 200 Gy and the third, whose 200 Gy row prints 75.86 % in both the lethality and the survival column, between 150 and 250 Gy.</onsir:boundQualifier>
    <skos:scopeNote>The source irradiated doses from 150 to 300 Gy; where the window extends past them, the position is arithmetic only.</skos:scopeNote>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Vigna unguiculata at or above LD50 dose</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/onsir/DoseCategory">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">dose category</rdfs:label>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="N946fc5efbf8d4ea7a8919a69037cb53e"/>
    <skos:definition>A qualitative classification of an irradiation dose by its predominant biological effect.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
